                    "message": "\ud83d\ude2d"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Are we planning to make this a PACKAGECONFIG or expect everyone to take on this dependency?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I think most systems have these in their image already, so I didn't think it made sense to make it a PACKAGECONFIG.  If you think there's systems that would opt out of this, we can make it a packageconfig and make the dependency optional, but that wasn't my plan."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I think I'm likely less concerned about the dependency and more about the added code size from a feature that will hopefully only be used on a few platforms."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "The difference in code size is 25kB for everything, likely <20KB if you dont include the refactor that happened in the same commit.  It didn't seem worth it to maintain an option for that.  FWIW, a lot of systems in the tree actually have this XML structure."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "@patrick@stwcx.xyz That work for you?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
